        "body": "In our code we use `ranges::nth_element` to partial sort the 10 highest doubles in a set of 2000, possibly containing infinity. Since version 0.13 however in some cases there is a crash.\r\n\r\nThe crash happens in `nth_element.hpp`, line 162. The code states `if (i == --j)`. `j` is the 0th element of the array however, resulting in a out of bounds write.\r\n\r\nI however did not succeed in reproducing the crash with a small example, so [RangesCrashExample.txt](https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/files/9626637/RangesCrashExample.txt) is a cpp-file with my example and the data used in our sorting algorithm.\r\nThis example has 2000 doubles with 8 entries `std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity()` and the comparison is `std::greater{}`.\r\n\r\nI compile using Visual Studio 16.11.19 with the MSVC 19.29 compiler.",
